WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.160
From 1993 to 2000, Boy Meets World&nbsp;
was a TGIF staple. The show shared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.040
a Friday primetime block with kid-friendly&nbsp;
sitcoms Family Matters and Step By Step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.680
When those two shows moved on, Boy Meets World&nbsp;
endured, sitting comfortably alongside Sabrina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.280
The Teenage Witch and various other&nbsp;
shows for the Friday primetime block.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.120
On Boy Meets World, Rider Strong played&nbsp;
Cory's best friend, Shawn Hunter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.360
In contrast to Cory's idyllic life, Shawn's&nbsp;
storylines often had the teenager grapple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.280
with some serious life issues. He was&nbsp;
abandoned by his stepmother several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.360
times and he lost his father soon&nbsp;
after they reunited, for starters.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.160
“It was all the things that you taught me that&nbsp;
made me wonder if it was the right place or not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.080
But you didn’t teach me enough.”

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.840
After Boy Meets World wrapped, the&nbsp;
world saw less and less of Strong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.080
He disappeared from television sets for&nbsp;
years until he reprised the role of Shawn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.760
all grown up, for Girl Meets World.&nbsp;
Years later, Strong opened up about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.160
why his presence became scarce. It turns out&nbsp;
the same storylines that made him memorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.240
have something to do with the reason why&nbsp;
Hollywood seemingly won't cast him anymore.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.040
In an interview with Vice, the&nbsp;
actor admitted that his desire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.880
to be considered a serious professional&nbsp;
clouded his judgment during his time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.880
on Boy Meets World. As an adult,&nbsp;
he now recognizes his aloofness.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.600
"I wanted to be a poet and academic writer. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.680
was definitely a period where I thought&nbsp;
I was way cooler than 'Boy Meets World.'"

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.840
As a result, the writers wrote more dramatic&nbsp;
storylines to keep the teenage Strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.840
interested in his role. Regardless of&nbsp;
their efforts, he was still miserable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.160
He didn't enjoy living up to the expectations&nbsp;
that came along with fame. He recalled one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.880
instance when he participated in a Sail With&nbsp;
the Stars charity cruise that left him scarred.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.600
Regarding the fans on the boat, Strong told Vice:

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.880
"They want a certain version of you,&nbsp;
whether that's Shawn Hunter or this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.680
perfect teen idol boyfriend, and suddenly,&nbsp;
you have to be that person 24 hours a day."

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.240
Strong nearly quit Boy Meets World soon after but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.800
finished the show's run with&nbsp;
the support of his parents.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.000
After Boy Meets World ended, Strong&nbsp;
enrolled at Columbia University,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.880
per his website. According to Mental Floss,&nbsp;
his famous classmates included Anna Paquin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.840
Julia Stiles, and Joseph Gordon-Levitt. Their&nbsp;
feature-film stardom meant he received less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:12.240
attention from the media while in school, which&nbsp;
he preferred. During his studies, Strong stayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:20.134
away from Hollywood, only taking one semester&nbsp;
off to film the indie horror hit Cabin Fever.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.840
He continued his education after&nbsp;
Columbia and earned an MFA in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.640
Fiction and Literature from Bennington College.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.680
Afterward, Strong returned to work&nbsp;
in the entertainment industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.880
Instead of television roles, he took on more&nbsp;
horror films, including 2017's Borderland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.720
Pulse 3, and Cabin Fever 2: Spring Fever. Finding&nbsp;
that he preferred to remain behind the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.800
Strong also began co-directing short films&nbsp;
with his brother. In between projects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.320
he also lends his voice to narrate&nbsp;
audiobooks. Since his reprisal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.560
Shawn Hunter on Girl Meets World, Strong has&nbsp;
added voiceover work to his list of credits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.360
including the Disney animated shows Mighty&nbsp;
Magiswords, and Star vs. The Forces of Evil.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.760
The next-gen spin-off Girl Meets World saw the&nbsp;
return of Rider Strong to network television.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.480
Although he was reluctant to return, he said&nbsp;
he was able to find a compromise with the show.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.040
"I knew that playing Shawn again&nbsp;
was going to be the final nail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.880
in the coffin of ever doing anything&nbsp;
else as an actor, so I did a trade."

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.760
Strong originally asked for seven episodes but&nbsp;
ended up directing 18 of them for the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.400
which ran for three seasons. Former co-stars&nbsp;
Ben Savage also directed a handful of Girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.840
Meets World episodes, bringing the&nbsp;
history of the show full circle.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.840
Strong is now a husband and father;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.368
he married actress Alexandra Barreto&nbsp;
in 2013 and they have one son.

